+# Changes, round 1
+
+All in src/statement.mjs. Capture rerun; npm test passes (3/3). Widest line is 61 characters.
+
+Closed:
+
+1. Ordering (major). Charges are sorted by amount, largest first, ties by service name (Key management before Load balancing). Credits are sorted largest credit first (Committed-use discount 410.63, then Service credit 164.25).
+2. Credits with a minus sign (major). Credits and the credits total are now written in parentheses, no minus sign. Plain amounts stop one column short of the table edge, so the closing parenthesis hangs in the last column and the decimal points stay in line.
+3. Zero-usage lines (major). Machine learning inference and Monitoring are dropped from the table. A sentence after the total says "2 services with no usage this month are not listed: Machine learning inference and Monitoring." Counts and names come from the data. The test that every service is named is still satisfied by this sentence.
+4. Share column (major). Each charge shows its percentage of total charges to one decimal (Compute 39.5%), computed with integer arithmetic, rounded half up. The Charges line shows 100.0%.
+5. Opening line and usage column (minor). The first line is the customer name with "Account NW-20418" right-aligned at the table edge; the month line is under it ("Usage statement, September 2026"). Quantity and unit are merged into one left-aligned "Usage" column ("18,250 vCPU-hours"). "Total due" no longer repeats the currency; USD appears once, in the "Amount (USD)" heading. The credits block drops its "Credits" heading line and the subtotal is labelled "Credits".
+
+Kept as before: rule-set total in the amount column, Charges line before credits, thousands commas, no currency signs, month by name, no trailing spaces, ASCII only.
+
+Left on purpose: nothing from GAPS.md. No conflict between GAPS.md, STYLE.md and tests/.
